{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Findings and verdicts (sandbox: 2 processes over one git store, each with its own `.rebar`, the blue-green view). Production check, read-only over SSM 2026-11-04: container rebar-mcp-1c8a67702f81-8093 started 08:58 PST, `/var/gerrit/site/.rebar` absent, tracker at `/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets`, process runs as root.\n\n- hlc.state / hlc.lock: no harm. With blue's cache 1 h ahead of the wall clock, blue wrote tkt-x at ahead+1. Green, with an empty cache, then ticked tkt-x at ahead+2: the witness floor (`_max_event_prefix`) comes from the shared tracker. Split caches gave equal ticks (both 1001 under a fixed clock) only when neither process had written in between, which means 2 concurrent events. `event_sort_key` orders those deterministically. Writers that see each other are serialized by `<tracker>/.ticket-write.lock`, which is shared. Left in place, with a comment in hlc.py.\n- recent-creates journal: harm. Blue recorded \"Fix the widget\". Blue's retry got a duplicate_warning; green's create of the same title got None. `verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets = true` in rebar.toml. Moved to `<git dir>/rebar-recent-creates.{json,lock}`.\n- similar-ticket index (`.rebar/cache/similar-tickets`): a cache rebuilt from the shared tracker. Left in place, with a comment in index.py.\n- compact-worker.log: already sent to stderr in the MCP container by `compact.worker_log` (3300). No change.\n\nTests: the new tests/unit/test_recent_creates_shared_journal.py failed 3 of 4 on main (the HLC pin passed, as expected) and passes 4 of 4 after the change. 212 targeted tests pass, and 599 across the create, clock, store, similar and mechanism modules (the mechanism baseline drained `lock::recent-creates.lock`). make lint and make typecheck exit 0. make verify: 20779 passed, 2 failed in tests/interfaces/facades. Both of those fail on the unchanged base as well and are already tracked as bald-diagnostic-cricket and fibre-beamy-angora."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793825594956870001,"uuid":"c465bb09-ee96-4c53-a800-7a91a9ff5e49"}